        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Vowel gotchas",
          "text": "- ou [u] is not u [y]: nous (we) vs nu (naked), tout vs tu. For u, round your lips and push them forward (you will practise it again in Leçon 13).\n- eu has two sounds: closed [ø] at the end of a word (peu, deux) and open [œ] before a consonant (peur, sœur, chanteur).\n- é is closed [e] (télé); è, ê and ai are open [ɛ] (mère, fête, j'ai). They sound close, but the difference matters in careful speech.\n- A letter combination is one sound, never letter by letter: eau is [o], not “e-a-u”."
        },
